Initial status: `video/storytime-song/scripts/render.mjs` and `dashboard/raw.json` are unrelated work of other sessions. They remain untouched. The untracked run outputs of other roles remain untouched.

Finding: the adversarial role on c8aba128, confirmed by the orchestrator. `storytimeQrUrl` (`dashboard/lib/storytime/files.ts:21`) checks only `startsWith('/th/st/')`. So `/th/st/../evil` is accepted, and a browser reads it as `https://storytime.reading-advantage.com/evil`. The week fields `home.songUrl` and `home.readAlongUrl` are free strings (`dashboard/lib/storytime/schema.ts:413-414`), so a wrong value reaches the printed QR code (spec P4, test-strategy line 363).

The rule of the orchestrator: the path is `/th/st/<level>/<week>` and then nothing, or one query `?part=book`, `?part=decodable`, or `?part=song`. The level is an integer from 1 to 4. The week is an integer from 1 to 32, with no leading zero. Every other path throws an error that names the path. The return value of an accepted path stays `STORYTIME_QR_HOST + pagePath`.

The tests: R48 adds 24 cases to `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-student-book.test.ts`.
- 22 reject cases: `/th/st/../evil`, `/th/st/../../evil`, `/th/st/2/./1`, `/th/st/2/1/..`, `/th/st//2/1`, `/th/st/`, `/th/st/2/1/3`, `/th/st/0/1`, `/th/st/5/1`, `/th/st/2/0`, `/th/st/2/33`, `/th/st/02/1`, `/th/st/2/01`, `/th/st/2/1 ` (space), `/th/st/2/1<TAB>`, `/th/st/2/1<NEWLINE>`, `/th/st/2/1#x`, `/th/st/2/1?week=2`, `/th/st/2/1?part=video`, `/th/st/2/1?part=song?part=book`, `/th/st/2/1?part=song&part=book`, `/th/st/2/1?part=SONG`. Each case fails at HEAD on the assertion that the call throws. The error message must name the path.
- 1 accept case: `/th/st/2/1`, `/th/st/2/1?part=song`, `/th/st/2/1?part=book`, `/th/st/2/1?part=decodable`, `/th/st/4/32`, `/th/st/1/1`. Each gives `STORYTIME_QR_HOST + path`. The case also holds that `/TH/st/2/1` throws; that case already holds at HEAD.
- 1 shipped-data case: the `home.songUrl` and the `home.readAlongUrl` of the 8 files `content/storytime/l2/w01.json` to `w08.json` pass `storytimeQrUrl`. The values are `/th/st/2/<n>?part=song`, `/th/st/2/<n>?part=book`, and `/th/st/2/8` for week 8. The case passes at HEAD and must keep passing.

