Type fix, commit 659c082c: the adversarial guard file `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-student-book-adversarial.test.ts` has a type error at HEAD df65ac05, at lines 235 and 257: `changedWeek(change, 30000)`, but the helper takes one argument. The fix removes the second argument from the two calls. It changes no expectation and no runtime value. The error was at HEAD before this Red work: a `npx tsc --noEmit` run with the Red change stashed gives the same two errors (`mid-red-df65ac05-tsc-head.txt`). The adversarial role ran `GREEN_TEST_COMMAND`, `PROJECT_TESTS`, and `PROJECT_LINT`, but not `PROJECT_CHECKS`, so the error was not seen. The orchestrator can revert that commit if the orchestrator prefers another owner for the fix.

Second round, on the decision of the orchestrator. The rule of Red 2i stays: only `?part=book`, `?part=decodable`, or `?part=song` is allowed. A hostile query is an input that the build must reject, not one that it escapes. The other A1 guards still cover the HTML escape of hostile week text.

Correction of commit 659c082c, in commit 39e721a0: the value 30000 is the test timeout of the two guards. The adversarial role put it in `changedWeek` and not in `it`. The commit 39e721a0 puts 30000 back as the third argument of `it(...)` for the guard A1 and for the guard A2, so both guards use the 30 s timeout and not the 5 s default.

Guard A1 change, in commit 39e721a0: the guard `A1: keeps a hostile QR query as text in the address attribute` becomes `A1: stops the build when the QR query is hostile`. Its assertion is `await expect(render(week)).rejects.toThrow('/th/st/2/1?part=song&x=<script>alert(1)</script>')`, in the same form as the `it.each` guard below it. The guard fails at HEAD, which is correct for Red. It passes after Green 2i.

